      <h1>about ‘apart’</h1>

      <p class="article-subtitle">
        a closer look at a piano-written ballad.
      </p>
    </header>


    <article class="article-content">

      <p><em>apart</em> is a piano-written ballad. over the course of these almost four minutes, different states of mind and moods unfold.</p>

      <p>i recorded the original piano part back in early 2025. ironically, it came from the very same wound that i would receive exactly one year later. it wasn't until this year that i rediscovered the recording and decided to work on it further.</p>

      <p><em>apart</em> is about distance. about the impossibility of getting close again. the desire to come closer and touch once more is immense. the heart wants it. but the mind understands that you cannot return to the source of your pain. and throughout the entire ballad, we witness this conflict.</p>

      <p>the first state is still bright, light, and pure. the heart is burning. then it moves into the next part — a blow. you don't understand what has happened yet, but you can feel that the thread that once held you together is growing weaker and is on the verge of breaking. the heart still doesn't understand what happened, while the mind already does. and gradually, everything descends into a kind of mourning. this moment is filled with uncertainty and doubt, but little by little, the heart begins to brighten and let go.</p>

      <p>yes, it happens very quickly, but the overall notes are there. the original recording is 15 minutes long, but i don't like most of it. the final composition consists of snippets from different parts of the recording, put together to convey the intended mood.</p>

      <p>the cover artwork features a photograph of a river taken by <a href="https://instagram.com/talk2medonttalk2me" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">talk2medonttalk2me</a>. it reflects the flow that runs throughout the composition.</p>

      <p><em>apart</em> was never intended to be part of <em>sonder</em>, and it won't be included on the upcoming debut album, either.</p>

